{
  "schema_version": 3,
  "_comment": "Canonical Fleet Core staffing data \u2014 the ONE authoring source for the model palette, the effort vocabulary, the work-shape tier policy, the per-vendor palette, the capability ratings and trust tiers, and the per-role staffing defaults (issue #1021). It absorbs the former models.json and tier_policy.json, which are deleted. models/efforts are the live Claude vocabulary for existing consumers (tier_palette.MODELS/EFFORTS, tier_resolver.resolve()). Do not treat them as the multi-vendor router. scalar_efforts, execution_classes, and root_orchestration_profiles are the portable subset shared with the Codex plugin repository, whose own copy stays at its schema_version 2 (KTD7); the subset is shared by content, not by version number; they are the authoritative execution-class policy. lineage_models/lineage_efforts are Codex compatibility data and are deliberately not ported. work_shapes is the work-shape -> tier registry that tier_resolver.load_policy() reads. vendors is the per-vendor palette that tier_resolver derives SUPPORTED_RUNTIMES, _RUNTIME_MODELS, _RUNTIME_ACCEPTED_EFFORTS, _EFFORT_COLLAPSE and _EFFORT_APPLICATION_MODE from. ORDERING IS LOAD-BEARING for models/efforts: rank 0 is the strongest model, rung 0 is the weakest effort. Grow the Claude vocabulary under models/efforts, never with a second bare literal elsewhere \u2014 see plugins/fleet-core/references/staffing.md.",
